
Revision history for Perl extension Net::Tools

1.60 (pending)

   - first Net-Tools release: socket modules split from Data::Tools 1.52 and
     renamed, Data::Tools::Socket* is now Net::Tools::Socket*:
              Net::Tools::Socket
              Net::Tools::Socket::Protocols
              Net::Tools::Socket::Pair
              Net::Tools::Socket::Err
     only the package names changed; earlier history is in Data::Tools
     Changes. the changes since Data::Tools 1.52 follow
   - added Net::Tools::Socket::Err, common error state for all socket
     modules: $SOCK_ERR (negative SOCK_E_* code or positive errno) and
     $SOCK_ERRSTR, sock_err(), sock_err_sys(), sock_err_name(),
     sock_err_clear()
   - added Net::Tools::Socket::Pair, SOCK_SEQPACKET socketpair messages,
     socketpair_create(), socketpair_send(), socketpair_recv();
     socketpair_create( 'dgram' ) creates SOCK_DGRAM pairs (no EOF on recv,
     a write end may be shared by many writers), see POD SOCKET TYPES;
     where MSG_NOSIGNAL is not available (macOS) socketpair_send() ignores
     SIGPIPE only during send(), the caller's handler is restored
   - INCOMPATIBLE: Net::Tools::Socket socket_read_message() returns the data
     only (no more list of data, length and error), undef on error, details
     are in $SOCK_ERR/$SOCK_ERRSTR (SOCK_E_EOF, SOCK_E_TIMEOUT,
     SOCK_E_TOOBIG, errno)
   - Net::Tools::Socket all functions set $SOCK_ERR on error, socket_write()
     and socket_write_message() refuse wide characters (SOCK_E_INVAL),
     EPIPE/ECONNRESET are reported as SOCK_E_EOF, EINTR is retried
   - Net::Tools::Socket socket_write_message() sends messages up to
     $WRITE_MESSAGE_JOIN_MAX (64 KiB) with one write, longer ones with two
     writes (length, then data, not copied), see POD about TCP_NODELAY
   - Net::Tools::Socket $timeout 0 does not wait at all (it waited forever
     before), undef waits forever
   - INCOMPATIBLE: Net::Tools::Socket::Protocols socket_protocol_read_message()
     returns ( $data, $ptype ) in list context and $data in scalar context,
     undef on error (no more error string), details in $SOCK_ERR/$SOCK_ERRSTR
     (SOCK_E_EMPTY, SOCK_E_PROTO, any socket error)
   - INCOMPATIBLE: Net::Tools::Socket::Protocols does not confess on unknown
     or forbidden protocol types and bad data anymore, read and write return
     undef with SOCK_E_PROTO or SOCK_E_INVAL, the stream stays in sync
   - INCOMPATIBLE: Net::Tools::Socket::Protocols 'p' (Storable) is unsafe on
     untrusted input, so it is forbidden by default and not allowed by '*',
     it must be allowed explicitly, e.g. socket_protocols_allow( '*p' )
   - Net::Tools::Socket::Protocols socket_protocols_allow() returns 1, types
     after '*' are added (they were ignored), unknown type confesses and
     keeps the allowed set; socket_protocol_read_message() takes $maxlen
   - tests for Socket::Err (t3) and Socket::Pair (t4), more socket and
     protocols tests
